+An ordinary single-node Passport relationship-list jump offers one `Back to`
+node action. It stores only the source node ID, replacing any earlier origin;
+returning consumes it. Preview and self-loops do not create an origin. Focus
+clearing or another semantic selection removes it, including Reach, Route,
+Lens, pinned relationships, multi-selection and hash restoration. Neither a
+missing nor an unrevealable hidden destination is selected; an unavailable return
+source removes the action while preserving the current selection. Collapsed tree
+ancestors expand through the existing tree reveal contract before selection. This does not
+restore camera, scroll or other reading state, and does not provide browser,
+Atlas or cross-diagram history. The control lives outside canonical SVG.
+
 Browser checks exercise actual node/relationship inputs, pointer delay, pin priority,
 Passport grouping, cyclic Reach and strict rejection, cold/hash URLs, copy feedback,
 real pulse end/cancel, media preference transitions, actual SVG export, three widths
